Package: samplesizeSimulation
Title: Simulation Based Sample Size Planning for Prediction Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Louis", "Chen", email = "chenaters@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates prediction performance across candidate sample sizes
    using simulated or resampled tabular data. Compares statistical and machine
    learning models with random or forward chaining validation, summarizes
    Monte Carlo variability, and reuses configuration matched simulation tables.
    Relative performance thresholds provide exploratory sample size
    recommendations under the specified data generating assumptions.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: MASS, stats, utils, graphics, grDevices, tools
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, mgcv, nnet, rpart,
    randomForest, gbm, e1071, glmnet, lme4, synthpop, pROC,
    ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), progress
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
